{"type":"message","id":"c8128fa7","parentId":"002a2310","timestamp":"2026-10-29T02:24:48.782Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_ig6hkJaVUnXqARsmzQ2H6461","toolName":"web_fetch","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Title: A People Map of the UK\nURL Source: https://pudding.cool/2019/06/people-map-uk/?x-respond-with=html\nMarkdown Content:\n**Hover** to see more details about each person.[](https://pudding.cool/2019/06/people-map-uk/?x-respond-with=html)\n#### Data and Methods\nData for this story were collected and processed using the [Wikipedia API](https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/API:Main_page). The period of collection was from July, 2015–May, 2019, from English Wikipedia. It was inspired in part by [this map](https://www.wearedorothy.com/collections/music/products/u-s-a-song-map-open-edition).\nPerson/city associations were based on the thousands of “People by city or town\" pages on Wikipedia. The top person from each city was determined by using median pageviews (with a minimum of 1 year of traffic). We chose to include multiple occurrences for a single person because there is both no way to determine which is more accurate and people can “be from” multiple places.\nGet in touch with us by email at sup@pudding.cool.\n\n## Links\n"}],"details":{},"isError":false,"timestamp":1793240688782}}
